{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared option lists, in one place, served at GET /api/v1/option-sets.",
    "",
    "These were hard-coded three times over in the source: in node_registry.py",
    "as _STATE_OPS / _MAPPING_TYPES / _SCHEMA_TYPES (which no node type actually",
    "referenced), again inside dynamic_fields.js where the list widgets built",
    "their own <select> options, and a third time in the HTML template and",
    "properties_panel.js. Adding an operation meant editing all three.",
    "",
    "Now the UI reads them from here. Adding an option is one line in this file.",
    "",
    "An option is {value, label} plus, where it earns one, a presentation or",
    "behaviour hint the UI would otherwise hard-code:",
    "  color          swatch, as node types already carry (variableTypes)",
    "  configurator   the dialog this choice opens, and configureLabel its",
    "                 wording — so no component tests for a particular value",
    "                 (toolTypes.mcp)"
  ],

  "mappingTypes": [
    { "value": "string",   "label": "String" },
    { "value": "number",   "label": "Number" },
    { "value": "boolean",  "label": "Boolean" },
    { "value": "array",    "label": "Array" },
    { "value": "object",   "label": "Object" },
    { "value": "variable", "label": "Variable Ref" }
  ],

